<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4867"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Speculation is cool and interesting and I do it all the time, but remember that BTK doesn&#39;t have a monopoly on Wichita area homicide. Reacting with horror to these possibles is playing right into BTK&#39;s hands. The burden is on BTK to prove he did any of these, not the other way round. I don&#39;t think he did one of &#39;em.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
